iables, None, None]. pushbyte 2, setlocal_2, getlocal_2, returnvalue -> 2.\n\nsetlocal_3/getlocal_3: local_count=3 -> registers = [variables, None, None, None]. pushbyte 3, setlocal_3, getlocal_3, returnvalue -> 3.\n\nunsupported opcode: bytes([255]) -> NotImplementedError. Also maybe another unknown like 100. One is enough.\n\nNow \u2014 the caching lines 833-834 and 442-443: after any successful run, extract_function stores resfunc. A second call to extract_function with the same (avm_class, func_name) returns the cached function (line 442-443). Let me add a test:\n\n```python\ndef test_extract_function_caches_resfunc():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = _AVMClass('(t)', 't')\n    avm_class.methods['f'] = _FakeMethod(bytes([OP_PUSHBYTE, 1, OP_RETURNVALUE]), 0)\n    f1 = interp.extract_function(avm_class, 'f')\n    f2 = interp.extract_function(avm_class, 'f')\n    assert f1 is f2\n    assert avm_class.method_pyfunctions['f'] is f1\n    assert f1([]) == 1\n```\n\nThis covers 833-834 and 442-443.\n\nNow, about `avm_class.methods` \u2014 need to confirm _AVMClass has `methods` dict. If not, I'll add `avm_class.methods = {}` in the helper. Let me check via get_info.\n\nAlso `method_names` \u2014 used in callproperty _ScopeDict branch and callpropvoid _ScopeDict branch. _AVMClass has method_names = {}.\n\nNow, one concern: `resfunc(args)` is called with a list. In `registers = [avm_class.variables] + list(args) + [None] * m.local_count`. Fine.\n\nAnother concern: `scopes = collections.deque([self._classes_by_name, avm_class.constants, avm_class.variables])`. `avm_class.constants` is a dict. Fine.\n\nNow, `findpropstrict` line 662: `for s in reversed(scopes)`. deque supports reversed. Good.\n\nNow let me also double-check the `callproperty` StringClass branch: `if obj == StringClass:`. _AVMClass.__eq__ compares self.name == other.name. obj is StringClass -> True.\n\nBut careful: in test (b) String(5): args[0] = 5 (int) -> res = compat_str(5) = '5'. Good.\n\nIn