 [8]=72. After reading s24 at position 6. offset=2 -> 8 -> returnvalue. Stack: [1]. Returns 1. \n\niftrue taken: [38] [17 s24(2)] [36 9] [72] -> returns True.\niftrue not taken: [39] [17 s24(2)] [36 9] [72] -> returns 9.\niffalse taken: [39] [18 s24(2)] [36 9] [72] -> returns False.\niffalse not taken: [38] [18 s24(2)] [36 9] [72] -> returns 9.\nifeq taken: [36 1] [36 1] [19 s24(2)] [36 9] [72] -> 1.\nifeq not taken: [36 1] [36 2] [19 s24(2)] [36 9] [72] -> 9.\nifne taken: [36 1] [36 2] [20 s24(2)] [36 9] [72] -> 1.\nifne not taken: [36 1] [36 1] [20 s24(2)] [36 9] [72] -> 9.\niflt taken: [36 1] [36 2] [21 s24(2)] [36 9] [72] -> 1.\niflt not taken: [36 2] [36 1] [21 s24(2)] [36 9] [72] -> 9.\n\npushnull: [32, 72] -> None.\npushundefined: [33, 72] -> is undefined.\npushbyte: [36, 42, 72] -> 42.\npushshort: [37] + u30(300) + [72] -> 300.\npushtrue: [38, 72] -> True.\npushfalse: [39, 72] -> False.\npushnan: [40, 72] -> math.isnan.\ndup: [36, 7, 42, 72] -> 7.\npushstring: [44] + u30(1) + [72] -> 'abc'.\npushscope: [36, 1, 42, 48, 72] -> 1. Wait: pushbyte 1, dup (42), pushscope (48) pops the dup -> scopes gets 1; stack still has original 1; returnvalue -> 1. Good.\n\nconstruct: getlex MyClass -> cls2 on stack; [96] + u30(IDX_MYCLASS) + [66] + u30(0) + [72] -> _AVMClass_Object with avm_class cls2.\n\nWait \u2014 construct: arg_count = u30(); args = reversed([stack.pop() for _ in range(arg_count)]); obj = stack.pop(); res = obj.avm_class.make_object(). With arg_count=0, args=[], obj=cls2. Good.\n\nHmm, but wait: getlex 'MyClass' \u2014 'MyClass' must be in _classes_by_name. Set interp._classes_by_name['MyClass'] = cls2. getlex: scopes reversed: variables (no), constants (no), _classes_by_name (yes) -> scope = _classes_by_name; 'MyClass' in scope -> res = cls2. Good.\n\ncallproperty tests:\n\na. String(undefined): [33] (pushundefined) + [93] + u30(IDX_STRING) (findpropstrict 'String') + [70] + u30(IDX_STRING) + u30(1) (callproperty 'String' 1) + [72].\n\nWait, order: pushundefined pushes undefined. findpropstrict pushes StringClass. callproperty: index=u30 -> mname='String'; arg_count=u30=1; args=[stack.pop()] = [undefined]; obj = stack.pop() = StringClass. obj == StringClass -> mname == 'String' -> args[0] == undefined -> res = 'undefined'. stack.append(res). continue. Then returnvalue -> 'undefined'. \n\nNote: `if obj == StringClass` \u2014 _AVMClass.__eq__ compares names. StringClass name is... whatever. obj is StringClass itself, so == is True.\n\nb. String(5): [36, 5] + findpropstrict + callproperty -> '5'.\n\nc. String('hi'): [44] + u30(IDX_HI) + findpropstrict + callproperty -> 'hi'.\n\nd. String.foo: findpropstrict 'String', callproperty IDX_UNKNOWN 0 -> NotImplementedError. Note: mname='unknownProp', obj=StringClass -> else branch raise NotImplementedError('Function String.unknownProp is not yet implemented').\n\ne. _AVMClass_Object call: \n```\ngetlex MyClass        -> cls2\nconstructproperty inst 0  -> obj\ncallproperty bar 0    -> calls cls2.methods['bar']\nreturnvalue\n```\ncls2.methods['bar'] = _FakeMethod(bytes([OP_PUSHBYTE, 99, OP_RETURNVALUE]), 0). Result 99.\n\nWait \u2014 extract_function(cls2, 'bar') \u2014 cls2.methods must contain 'bar'. And after extraction, cls2.method_pyfunctions['bar'] = resfunc. Fine.\n\nf. _AVMClass call: getlex MyClass, callproperty baz 0 -> cls2.methods['baz'] = pushbyte 77, returnvalue -> 77.\n\ng. _ScopeDict with method_names: findproperty IDX_NOPE -> pushes avm_class.variables. callproperty IDX_M1 0. avm_class.method_names['m1'] = something; avm_class.methods['m1'] = _FakeMethod(pushbyte 55, returnvalue). Result 55.\n\nWait \u2014 findproperty: mname='nope' not in any scope -> res = avm_class.variables. Then callproperty: obj = variables (a _ScopeDict), mname='m1' in obj.avm_class.method_names -> func = extract_function(avm_class, 'm1'). Good.\n\nh. _ScopeDict without method_names: avm_class.constants['k'] = 42. findproperty IDX_NOPE, callproperty IDX_K 0 -> obj['k'] -> _ScopeDict.__getitem__ -> constants['k'] = 42. Result 42.\n\ni. split(''): pushstring 'abc' (idx 1), pushstring '' (idx 0), callproperty IDX_SPLIT 1 -> list('abc') = ['a','b','c'].\n\nj. split(','): pushstring 'a,b' (idx 2), pushstring ',' (idx 3), callproperty IDX_SPLIT 1 -> ['a','b'].\n\nk. charCodeAt: pushstring 'abc', pushbyte 1, callproperty IDX_CHARCODEAT 1 -> 98.\n\nl. slice: pushbyte 1, pushbyte 2, newarray 2 -> [1,2]; pushbyte 1, callproperty IDX_SLICE 1 -> [2].\n\nm. join: pushstring 'a', pushstring 'b', newarray 2 -> ['a','b']; pushstring ',' (idx 3), callproperty IDX_JOIN 1 -> 'a,b'.\n\nn. unsupported: pushbyte 1, callproperty IDX_UNKNOWN 0 -> NotImplementedError('Unsupported property ...').\n\nreturnvoid: [36, 1, 71] -> undefined.\n\nconstructsuper: [36, 7, 36, 1, 36, 2, 73] + u30(2) + [36, 3, 72] -> 3.\n\nconstructproperty: covered in (e). Also assert isinstance.\n\ncallpropvoid:\na. object: getlex MyClass, constructproperty inst 0, callpropvoid voidm 0, then pushbyte 1, returnvalue -> 1. cls2.methods['voidm'] = _FakeMethod(bytes([OP_RETURNVOID]), 0). res = undefined -> assert passes.\nb. scopedict: findproperty nope, callpropvoid m2 0, pushbyte 1, returnvalue -> 1. avm_class.method_names['m2'] = 'm2'; avm_class.methods['m2'] = returnvoid code.\nc. reverse: pushbyte 1, pushbyte 2, newarray 2, dup, callpropvoid reverse 0, returnvalue -> [2,1].\nd. unsupported: pushbyte 1, callpropvoid IDX_UNKNOWN 0 -> NotImplementedError.\n\nnewarray: pushbyte 1, pushbyte 2, newarray 2, returnvalue -> [1, 2]. Note arr built by popping: [2,1] then reversed -> [1,2]. Good.\n\nfindpropstrict:\na. in variables: avm_class.variables['x'] = 5; findpropstrict IDX... wait 'x' needs to be in multinames. Hmm, I didn't include 'x'. Let me add 'x' and 'y', 'z' to multinames. Or reuse 'zz'/'key'. Let me just add more names. I'll extend the multinames list:\n\n```\n'x',   # 23\n'y',   # 24\n'z',   # 25\n```\n\nfindpropstrict 'x' -> res = variables; 'x' in res -> res['x'] = 5. returnvalue -> 5.\n\nb.