bles, None, None]. pushbyte 2, setlocal_2, getlocal_2, returnvalue -> 2.\n\nsetlocal_3/getlocal_3: local_count=3 -> registers = [variables, None, None, None]. pushbyte 3, setlocal_3, getlocal_3, returnvalue -> 3.\n\nunsupported opcode: bytes([255]) -> NotImplementedError. Also maybe another unknown like 100. One is enough.\n\nNow \u2014 the caching lines 833-834 and 442-443: after any successful run, extract_function stores resfunc. A second call to extract_function with the same (avm_class, func_name) returns the cached function (line 442-443). Let me add a test:\n\n```python\ndef test_extract_function_caches_resfunc():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = _AVMClass('(t)', 't')\n    avm_class.methods['f'] = _FakeMethod(bytes([OP_PUSHBYTE, 1, OP_RETURNVALUE]), 0)\n    f1 = interp.extract_function(avm_class, 'f')\n    f2 = interp.extract_function(avm_class, 'f')\n    assert f1 is f2\n    assert avm_class.method_pyfunctions['f'] is f1\n    assert f1([]) == 1\n```\n\nThis covers 833-834 and 442-443.\n\nNow, about `avm_class.methods` \u2014 need to confirm _AVMClass has `methods` dict. If not, I'll add `avm_class.methods = {}` in the helper. Let me check via get_info.\n\nAlso `method_names` \u2014 used in callproperty _ScopeDict branch and callpropvoid _ScopeDict branch. _AVMClass has method_names = {}.\n\nNow, one concern: `resfunc(args)` is called with a list. In `registers = [avm_class.variables] + list(args) + [None] * m.local_count`. Fine.\n\nAnother concern: `scopes = collections.deque([self._classes_by_name, avm_class.constants, avm_class.variables])`. `avm_class.constants` is a dict. Fine.\n\nNow, `findpropstrict` line 662: `for s in reversed(scopes)`. deque supports reversed. Good.\n\nNow let me also double-check the `callproperty` StringClass branch: `if obj == StringClass:`. _AVMClass.__eq__ compares self.name == other.name. obj is StringClass -> True.\n\nBut careful: in test (b) String(5): args[0] = 5 (int) -> res = compat_str(5) = '5'. Good.\n\nIn test (c): args[0] = 'hi' -> 'hi'.\n\nWhat about `assert isinstance(args[0], (int, compat_str, _Undefined))` \u2014 undefined is _Undefined instance. Good.\n\nNow the `construct` opcode (66): `res = obj.avm_class.make_object()`. obj must have avm_class attr. cls2 is _AVMClass \u2014 does _AVMClass have `.avm_class`? No! _AVMClass doesn't have avm_class attribute... wait, line 526: `res = obj.avm_class.make_object()`. If obj is an _AVMClass, obj.avm_class would raise AttributeError unless _AVMClass has that attribute. Hmm!\n\nLet me re-read: \n\n```python\nelif opcode == 66:  # construct\n    arg_count = u30()\n    args = list(reversed(\n        [stack.pop() for _ in range(arg_count)]))\n    obj = stack.pop()\n    res = obj.avm_class.make_object()\n    stack.append(res)\n```\n\nSo obj must be an _AVMClass_Object (which has .avm_class). So for construct, I need an _AVMClass_Object on the stack. How? getlex of a class gives _AVMClass, not object. Hmm.\n\nOption: push an _AVMClass_Object via... constructproperty creates one. So: getlex MyClass -> cls2; constructproperty inst 0 -> obj (AVMClass_Object); then construct 0 -> obj.avm_class.make_object() -> new object. \n\nSo code: getlex MyClass, constructproperty IDX_INST 0, construct 0, returnvalue -> _AVMClass_Object with avm_class cls2. That covers 66.\n\nAlternatively, does _AVMClass have an `avm_class` attribute? Let me check the real code... I believe _AVMClass does NOT have avm_class. So use the two-step approach.\n\nHmm wait, actually maybe I should double check whether _AVMClass defines `avm_class`... The get_info call will show the class source.\n\nNow `constructproperty` (74): `assert isinstance(obj, _AVMClass)` \u2014 obj is cls2. Good.\n\nNow, about `pushscope` (48): pops value and appends to scopes. Fine.\n\nNow `coerce_s` (133): `assert isinstance(stack[-1], (type(None), compat_str))`. pushnull -> None -> passes. pushstring -> str -> passes.\n\nNow `getproperty` length branch: `assert isinstance(obj, (compat_str, list))`. pushstring 'abc' -> str. Good.\n\nNow, one more thing: the `run` helper calls `func(list(args))` \u2014 resfunc(args). args default ().\n\nNow let me also think about whether `extract_function` might hit `self._classes_by_name[func_name].make_object()` \u2014 line 445 \u2014 covered by test 3.\n\nNow, potential issue: `_AVMClass.__init__` signature: `_AVMClass(name, resolved_name, class_body=None)`. I'll call `_AVMClass('(t)', 't')`.\n\nLet me now also handle: does `extract_function` get called with func_name that's in `avm_class.methods`? Yes, we set methods.\n\nNow, the multinames list: `self.multinames[index]` \u2014 index from u30. Our list must be long enough.\n\nAlso `self.constant_strings[idx]` for pushstring.\n\nNow let me write the final test file. But first, get_info calls to confirm the internals. Let me batch:\n\n1. get_info(\"SWFInterpreter\")\n2. get_info(\"_AVMClass\")\n3. get_info(\"_AVMClass_Object\")\n4. get_info(\"_ScopeDict\")\n5. get_info(\"_Multiname\")\n6. get_info(\"_Undefined\")\n7. get_info(\"undefined\")\n8. get_info(\"_builtin_classes\")\n9. get_info(\"StringClass\")\n10. get_info(\"_read_byte\")\n11. get_info(\"_u30\")\n12. get_info(\"_s24\")\n\nLet me do that.\n\nAfter that, I'll write the test file accordingly.\n\nOne more consideration: the test file should import from `youtube_dl.swfinterp`. If some names are private, they're still importable.\n\nAlso need `pytest.raises(NotImplementedError)` and `ExtractorError`.\n\nCleanup/state pollution: We create fresh interpreter and avm_class objects per test \u2014 no global state modified. We don't monkeypatch anything global. The `_builtin_classes` and `StringClass` are module-level but we don't modify them. So no cleanup needed beyond fresh fixtures. Good.\n\nLet me also think about `_u30` decoding: if implemented as:\n\n```python\ndef _u30(coder):\n    v = _read_uint(coder)\n    assert v < 2**31  # or something\n    return v\n```\n\nand `_read_uint`:\n\n```python\ndef _read_uint(coder):\n    n = 0\n    shift = 0\n    while True:\n        b = coder.read(1)[0]\n        n = n | ((b & 0x7f) << shift)\n        if not b & 0x80:\n            break\n        shift += 7\n    return n\n```\n\nMy encoder (little-endian 7-bit groups with continuation bit) matches this. If instead it's big-endian style (`n = (n << 7) | (b & 0x7f)`), my encoder would be wrong. get_info will tell. The ABC format uses little-endian 7-bit groups, and youtube_dl's implementation... let me recall the actual swfinterp.py:\n\n```python\ndef _read_byte(coder):\n    return coder.read(1)[0]\n\n\ndef _read_uint(coder):\n    n = 0\n    shift = 0\n    while True:\n        b = coder.read(1)[0]\n        n |= (b & 0x7f) << shift\n        if not b & 0x80:\n            break\n        shift += 7\n    return n\n\n\ndef _s24(coder):\n    bs = coder.read(3)\n    if bs[2] & 0x80:\n        v = -((bs[0] | (bs[1] << 8) | ((bs[2] & 0x7f) << 16)) ...\n```\n\nHmm, I don't remember exactly. Let me just query.\n\nActually, I recall from youtube_dl swfinterp.py:\n\n```python\ndef _read_byte(coder):\n    return coder.read(1)[0]\n\n\ndef _read_uint(coder):\n    n = 0\n    for i in range(5):\n        b = coder.read(1)[0]\n        n = (n << 7) | (b & 0x7f)\n        if not b & 0x80:\n            break\n    return n\n```\n\nHmm no. Let me actually think about the real source. From youtube-dl master swfinterp.py:\n\n```python\ndef _read_byte(coder):\n    return coder.read(1)[0]\n\n\ndef _read_uint(coder):\n    n = 0\n    shift = 0\n    while True:\n        b = _read_byte(coder)\n        n |= (b & 0x7f) << shift\n        if not (b & 0x80):\n            break\n        shift += 7\n    return n\n\n\ndef _s24(coder):\n    b = coder.read(3)\n    v = b[0] | (b[1] << 8) | (b[2] << 16)\n    if v & 0x800000:\n        v -= 0x1000000\n    return v\n\n\ndef _u30(coder):\n    v = _read_uint(coder)\n    assert v & 0xf0000000 == 0\n    return v\n```\n\nI'm fairly confident it's little-endian 7-bit groups (standard AVM2 u30). And s24 is 3-byte little-endian two's complement. My encoders match. But let me verify with get_info anyway.\n\nNow, let me also consider: `pushshort` uses u30 \u2014 value 300 encodes as: 300 = 0b100101100 -> low 7 bits: 0101100 (0x2C) with continuation, next: 10 (0x02). So bytes: 0xAC, 0x02. My u30(300) produces that.\n\nNow, writing the final test script. Structure:\n\n```python\nimport itertools\nimport math\n\nimport pytest\n\nimport youtube_dl.swfinterp as swfinterp\nfrom youtube_dl.swfinterp import (\n    SWFInterpreter,\n    _AVMClass,\n    _AVMClass_Object,\n    _ScopeDict,\n    _Multiname,\n    undefined,\n    _builtin_classes,\n    StringClass,\n)\nfrom youtube_dl.utils import ExtractorError\n```\n\nHmm, importing private names \u2014 fine.\n\nOpcode constants and helpers as discussed.\n\nLet me now also double check `callproperty` when obj is _ScopeDict and mname in method_names: `func = self.extract_function(obj.avm_class, mname)`. obj.avm_class is avm_class. extract_function(avm_class, 'm1') -> avm_class.methods['m1']. Good.\n\nAnd callpropvoid _ScopeDict branch: `assert mname in obj.avm_class.method_names`. So avm_class.method_names must contain 'm2'. Set `avm_class.method_names['m2'] = 'm2'` (value irrelevant).\n\nSimilarly for callproperty _ScopeDict branch: `if mname in obj.avm_class.method_names:` \u2014 set method_names['m1'].\n\nNow, about `findproperty` returning avm_class.variables when not found \u2014 note that `avm_class.variables` is a _ScopeDict whose avm_class is avm_class. Good.\n\nNow, `setproperty` with obj = variables: `obj[idx] = value` \u2014 _ScopeDict inherits dict __setitem__. Good.\n\nNow let me think about whether `getlex` for 'MyClass' works: scopes reversed: [variables, constants, _classes_by_name]. 'MyClass' in variables? variables is _ScopeDict \u2014 `in` checks dict keys. No. constants \u2014 no. _classes_by_name \u2014 yes. scope = _classes_by_name. `if mname in scope: res = scope[mname]` -> cls2. Good.\n\nNow `construct` after constructproperty: stack has _AVMClass_Object; construct 0: obj = that object; res = obj.avm_class.make_object(). Good.\n\nNow, let me write out all tests. I'll aim for compact but complete. Let me also add a parametrized test for arithmetic ops to reduce repetition? The instructions want test functions; parametrize is fine.\n\nLet me write:\n\n```python\nimport itertools\nimport math\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom youtube_dl.swfinterp import (\n    SWFInterpreter,\n    _AVMClass,\n    _AVMClass_Object,\n    _ScopeDict,\n    _Multiname,\n    undefined,\n    _builtin_classes,\n    StringClass,\n)\nfrom youtube_dl.utils import ExtractorError\n\n\n# --- bytecode encoding helpers -------------------------------------------\n\ndef u30(value):\n    parts = bytearray()\n    while True:\n        b = value & 0x7F\n        value >>= 7\n        if value:\n            parts.append(b | 0x80)\n        else:\n            parts.append(b)\n            return bytes(parts)\n\n\ndef s24(value):\n    if value < 0:\n        value += 1 << 24\n    return bytes((value & 0xFF, (value >> 8) & 0xFF, (value >> 16) & 0xFF))\n\n\ndef code(*parts):\n    out = bytearray()\n    for p in parts:\n        if isinstance(p, int):\n            out.append(p)\n        else:\n            out.extend(p)\n    return bytes(out)\n```\n\nOpcodes:\n\n```python\nLABEL = 9\nJUMP = 16\nIFTRUE = 17\nIFFALSE = 18\nIFEQ = 19\nIFNE = 20\nIFLT = 21\nPUSHNULL = 32\nPUSHUNDEFINED = 33\nPUSHBYTE = 36\nPUSHSHORT = 37\nPUSHTRUE = 38\nPUSHFALSE = 39\nPUSHNAN = 40\nDUP = 42\nPUSHSTRING = 44\nPUSHSCOPE = 48\nCONSTRUCT = 66\nCALLPROPERTY = 70\nRETURNVOID = 71\nRETURNVALUE = 72\nCONSTRUCTSUPER = 73\nCONSTRUCTPROPERTY = 74\nCALLPROPVOID = 79\nNEWARRAY = 86\nFINDPROPSTRICT = 93\nFINDPROPERTY = 94\nGETLEX = 96\nSETPROPERTY = 97\nGETLOCAL = 98\nSETLOCAL = 99\nGETPROPERTY = 102\nINITPROPERTY = 104\nCONVERT_I = 115\nCOERCE = 128\nCOERCE_A = 130\nCOERCE_S = 133\nDECREMENT = 147\nTYPEOF = 149\nADD = 160\nSUBTRACT = 161\nMULTIPLY = 162\nMODULO = 164\nBITAND = 168\nEQUALS = 171\nGREATEREQUALS = 175\nINCREMENT_I = 192\nGETLOCAL0 = 208\nGETLOCAL1 = 209\nGETLOCAL2 = 210\nGETLOCAL3 = 211\nSETLOCAL1 = 213\nSETLOCAL2 = 214\nSETLOCAL3 = 215\n```\n\nMultiname indices:\n\n```python\n(\n    'length', 'split', 'charCodeAt', 'slice', 'join', 'String',\n    'reverse', 'unknownProp', 'bar', 'baz', 'm1', 'k', 'voidm', 'm2',\n    'sp', 'zz', 'ip', 'key', 'key2', 'inst', 'MyClass', 'nope',\n    'x', 'y', 'z',\n)\n```\n\nIndices:\n0 length\n1 split\n2 charCodeAt\n3 slice\n4 join\n5 String\n6 reverse\n7 unknownProp\n8 bar\n9 baz\n10 m1\n11 k\n12 voidm\n13 m2\n14 sp\n15 zz\n16 ip\n17 key\n18 key2\n19 inst\n20 MyClass\n21 nope\n22 x\n23 y\n24 z\n25 _Multiname (dynamic)\n\nConstant strings:\n\n```python\nSTRINGS = ['', 'abc', 'a,b', ',', 'hi', 'x', 'key', 'key2', '42']\nS_EMPTY, S_ABC, S_AB, S_COMMA, S_HI, S_X, S_KEY, S_KEY2, S_42 = range(9)\n```\n\nFixtures/helpers:\n\n```python\n_counter = itertools.count()\n\n\nclass _FakeMethod(object):\n    def __init__(self, code_bytes, local_count=0):\n        self.code = code_bytes\n        self.local_count = local_count\n\n\ndef make_interp():\n    interp = SWFInterpreter.__new__(SWFInterpreter)\n    interp._classes_by_name = {}\n    interp.constant_strings = list(STRINGS)\n    interp.multinames = list(MULTINAMES)\n    interp._patched_functions = {}\n    return interp\n\n\ndef make_avm_class():\n    avm_class = _AVMClass('(test)', 'test')\n    if not hasattr(avm_class, 'methods'):\n        avm_class.methods = {}\n    return avm_class\n\n\ndef run(interp, avm_class, code_bytes, local_count=0, args=()):\n    name = 'f%d' % next(_counter)\n    avm_class.methods[name] = _FakeMethod(code_bytes, local_count)\n    func = interp.extract_function(avm_class, name)\n    return func(list(args))\n```\n\nHmm wait \u2014 if `_AVMClass.__init__` already defines `methods`, the hasattr check is harmless. But if it doesn't, we need it. Actually, let me check via get_info first and then decide. I'll include the hasattr guard regardless \u2014 it's safe.\n\nHmm, but actually if `methods` doesn't exist as attribute, `extract_function` line 446 `if func_name not in avm_class.methods` would fail with AttributeError. The guard handles it.\n\nNow the tests:\n\n```python\ndef test_extract_function_patched_function():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    sentinel = lambda args: 'patched-result'\n    interp._patched_functions[(avm_class, 'f')] = sentinel\n    assert interp.extract_function(avm_class, 'f') is sentinel\n\n\ndef test_extract_function_pyfunction():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    avm_class.method_pyfunctions['f'] = lambda args: 'py-result'\n    assert interp.extract_function(avm_class, 'f')([]) == 'py-result'\n\n\ndef test_extract_function_class_name_returns_object():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    other = _AVMClass('(other)', 'other')\n    interp._classes_by_name['ctor'] = other\n    obj = interp.extract_function(avm_class, 'ctor')\n    assert isinstance(obj, _AVMClass_Object)\n    assert obj.avm_class is other\n\n\ndef test_extract_function_missing_function_raises():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    with pytest.raises(ExtractorError) as exc_info:\n        interp.extract_function(avm_class, 'missing')\n    assert 'test.missing' in str(exc_info.value)\n```\n\nHmm, the error message: 'Cannot find function %s.%s' % (avm_class.name, func_name) -> 'Cannot find function (test).missing'. avm_class.name = '(test)'. So assert '(test).missing' in str. OK.\n\n```python\ndef test_extract_function_caches_generated_function():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    avm_class.methods['f'] = _FakeMethod(code(PUSHBYTE, 1, RETURNVALUE))\n    first = interp.extract_function(avm_class, 'f')\n    second = interp.extract_function(avm_class, 'f')\n    assert first is second\n    assert avm_class.method_pyfunctions['f'] is first\n    assert first([]) == 1\n```\n\nOpcode tests:\n\n```python\ndef test_opcode_label_does_nothing():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(PUSHBYTE, 5, LABEL, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 5\n\n\ndef test_opcode_jump_taken():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHBYTE, 1, JUMP, s24(2), PUSHBYTE, 9, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 1\n\n\ndef test_opcode_iftrue():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    taken = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHTRUE, IFTRUE, s24(2), PUSHBYTE, 9, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert taken is True\n    not_taken = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHFALSE, IFTRUE, s24(2), PUSHBYTE, 9, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert not_taken == 9\n```\n\netc.\n\nLet me write all of them. Also negative jump offset test? `s24` negative: jump backwards could infinite-loop; skip. But to cover the sign handling of s24... the s24 function itself is not in the uncovered range (it's a module-level helper, presumably covered elsewhere or not \u2014 the task says lines 439-834). Negative offsets aren't needed.\n\nNow, typeof returns directly \u2014 note that after `return {...}[type(value)]`, lines 833-834 are NOT executed for that path (return inside loop). That's fine; other tests cover 833-834.\n\nWait, actually \u2014 important: `return` inside the while loop exits resfunc, so lines 833-834 only execute if the while loop exits normally... but the while loop only exits via return statements (returnvoid/returnvalue/typeof) or exceptions. So how is line 833-834 ever reached?! Let me re-read.\n\n```python\n            while True:\n                opcode = _read_byte(coder)\n                ...\n                elif opcode == 71:  # returnvoid\n                    res = undefined\n                    return res\n                elif opcode == 72:  # returnvalue\n                    res = stack.pop()\n                    return res\n                ...\n                else:\n                    raise NotImplementedError(...)\n\n        avm_class.method_pyfunctions[func_name] = resfunc\n        return resfunc\n```\n\nThe `while True` loop is inside `resfunc`. The lines 833-834 are at the level of `extract_function`, after the definition of resfunc \u2014 they execute when `extract_function` is called, regardless of resfunc's internals. The indentation: `avm_class.method_pyfunctions[func_name] = resfunc` is at the `def resfunc(args):` level (8 spaces? no...). Looking at the snippet: line 833 `        avm_class.method_pyfunctions[func_name] = resfunc` \u2014 8 spaces, same level as `def resfunc` (8 spaces? `def resfunc(args):` at line 451 has 8 spaces). Yes, so 833-834 execute after defining resfunc, when extract_function runs. Every extract_function call that reaches the method-parsing path executes 833-834. Good \u2014 covered by all opcode tests.\n\nNow, the `while True` loop inside resfunc: every opcode test executes the loop. Good.\n\nNow let me also double check `run` for tests where code ends with RETURNVOID \u2014 resfunc returns undefined.\n\nNow, `test_opcode_pushundefined`: res is undefined \u2014 `assert res is undefined`.\n\n`test_opcode_pushnan`: `assert isinstance(res, float) and math.isnan(res)`.\n\nNow the callproperty tests in detail:\n\n```python\ndef test_callproperty_string_class_from_undefined():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHUNDEFINED,\n        FINDPROPSTRICT, u30(IDX_STRING),\n        CALLPROPERTY, u30(IDX_STRING), u30(1),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 'undefined'\n```\n\nWait \u2014 findpropstrict 'String': 'String' not in variables/constants/_classes_by_name -> res = scopes[0] = _classes_by_name; 'String' not in res and 'String' in _builtin_classes -> push _builtin_classes['String'] = StringClass. Then callproperty: obj = StringClass. `if obj == StringClass:` -> True. mname = 'String'. args = [undefined]. res = 'undefined'. \n\n```python\ndef test_callproperty_string_class_from_int():\n    ... PUSHBYTE, 5 ... -> '5'\n\ndef test_callproperty_string_class_from_str():\n    ... PUSHSTRING, u30(S_HI) ... -> 'hi'\n\ndef test_callproperty_string_class_unsupported_method():\n    with pytest.raises(NotImplementedError) as exc_info:\n        run(interp, avm_class, code(\n            FINDPROPSTRICT, u30(IDX_STRING),\n            CALLPROPERTY, u30(IDX_UNKNOWN), u30(0),\n            RETURNVALUE))\n    assert 'String.unknownProp' in str(exc_info.value)\n```\n\nObject call:\n\n```python\ndef test_callproperty_on_avm_class_object():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    other = make_avm_class()\n    other.methods['bar'] = _FakeMethod(code(PUSHBYTE, 99, RETURNVALUE))\n    interp._classes_by_name['MyClass'] = other\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        GETLEX, u30(IDX_MYCLASS),\n        CONSTRUCTPROPERTY, u30(IDX_INST), u30(0),\n        CALLPROPERTY, u30(IDX_BAR), u30(0),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 99\n```\n\nClass call:\n\n```python\ndef test_callproperty_on_avm_class():\n    ...\n    other.methods['baz'] = _FakeMethod(code(PUSHBYTE, 77, RETURNVALUE))\n    res = run(..., code(\n        GETLEX, u30(IDX_MYCLASS),\n        CALLPROPERTY, u30(IDX_BAZ), u30(0),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 77\n```\n\nScopeDict with method:\n\n```python\ndef test_callproperty_on_scope_dict_with_method():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    avm_class.method_names['m1'] = 'm1'\n    avm_class.methods['m1'] = _FakeMethod(code(PUSHBYTE, 55, RETURNVALUE))\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        FINDPROPERTY, u30(IDX_NOPE),\n        CALLPROPERTY, u30(IDX_M1), u30(0),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 55\n```\n\nScopeDict without method:\n\n```python\ndef test_callproperty_on_scope_dict_constant():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    avm_class.constants['k'] = 42\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        FINDPROPERTY, u30(IDX_NOPE),\n        CALLPROPERTY, u30(IDX_K), u30(0),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 42\n```\n\nWait \u2014 `res = obj[mname]` where obj is _ScopeDict -> __getitem__ -> constants['k'] = 42. Good.\n\nString split:\n\n```python\ndef test_callproperty_string_split_empty_separator():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHSTRING, u30(S_ABC),\n        PUSHSTRING, u30(S_EMPTY),\n        CALLPROPERTY, u30(IDX_SPLIT), u30(1),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == ['a', 'b', 'c']\n\n\ndef test_callproperty_string_split_separator():\n    res = run(..., code(\n        PUSHSTRING, u30(S_AB),\n        PUSHSTRING, u30(S_COMMA),\n        CALLPROPERTY, u30(IDX_SPLIT), u30(1),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == ['a', 'b']\n\n\ndef test_callproperty_string_char_code_at():\n    res = run(..., code(\n        PUSHSTRING, u30(S_ABC),\n        PUSHBYTE, 1,\n        CALLPROPERTY, u30(IDX_CHARCODEAT), u30(1),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 98\n```\n\nList slice/join:\n\n```python\ndef test_callproperty_list_slice():\n    res = run(..., code(\n        PUSHBYTE, 1, PUSHBYTE, 2,\n        NEWARRAY, u30(2),\n        PUSHBYTE, 1,\n        CALLPROPERTY, u30(IDX_SLICE), u30(1),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == [2]\n\n\ndef test_callproperty_list_join():\n    res = run(..., code(\n        PUSHSTRING, u30(S_ABC), PUSHSTRING, u30(S_X),\n        NEWARRAY, u30(2),\n        PUSHSTRING, u30(S_COMMA),\n        CALLPROPERTY, u30(IDX_JOIN), u30(1),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 'abc,x'\n```\n\nUnsupported:\n\n```python\ndef test_callproperty_unsupported_property_raises():\n    with pytest.raises(NotImplementedError) as exc_info:\n        run(interp, avm_class, code(\n            PUSHBYTE, 1,\n            CALLPROPERTY, u30(IDX_UNKNOWN), u30(0),\n            RETURNVALUE))\n    assert 'unknownProp' in str(exc_info.value)\n```\n\nreturnvoid:\n\n```python\ndef test_opcode_returnvoid():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(PUSHBYTE, 1, RETURNVOID))\n    assert res is undefined\n```\n\nconstructsuper:\n\n```python\ndef test_opcode_constructsuper():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHBYTE, 7, PUSHBYTE, 1, PUSHBYTE, 2,\n        CONSTRUCTSUPER, u30(2),\n        PUSHBYTE, 3, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 3\n```\n\nconstruct:\n\n```python\ndef test_opcode_construct():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    other = make_avm_class()\n    interp._classes_by_name['MyClass'] = other\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        GETLEX, u30(IDX_MYCLASS),\n        CONSTRUCTPROPERTY, u30(IDX_INST), u30(0),\n        CONSTRUCT, u30(0),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert isinstance(res, _AVMClass_Object)\n    assert res.avm_class is other\n```\n\nconstructproperty is covered here too, but let me have a dedicated one:\n\n```python\ndef test_opcode_constructproperty():\n    ...\n    res = run(..., code(\n        GETLEX, u30(IDX_MYCLASS),\n        CONSTRUCTPROPERTY, u30(IDX_INST), u30(0),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert isinstance(res, _AVMClass_Object)\n    assert res.avm_class is other\n```\n\ncallpropvoid:\n\n```python\ndef test_callpropvoid_on_avm_class_object():\n    other.methods['voidm'] = _FakeMethod(code(RETURNVOID))\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        GETLEX, u30(IDX_MYCLASS),\n        CONSTRUCTPROPERTY, u30(IDX_INST), u30(0),\n        CALLPROPVOID, u30(IDX_VOIDM), u30(0),\n        PUSHBYTE, 1, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 1\n\n\ndef test_callpropvoid_on_scope_dict():\n    avm_class.method_names['m2'] = 'm2'\n    avm_class.methods['m2'] = _FakeMethod(code(RETURNVOID))\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        FINDPROPERTY, u30(IDX_NOPE),\n        CALLPROPVOID, u30(IDX_M2), u30(0),\n        PUSHBYTE, 1, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 1\n\n\ndef test_callpropvoid_reverse():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHBYTE, 1, PUSHBYTE, 2,\n        NEWARRAY, u30(2),\n        DUP,\n        CALLPROPVOID, u30(IDX_REVERSE), u30(0),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == [2, 1]\n\n\ndef test_callpropvoid_unsupported_raises():\n    with pytest.raises(NotImplementedError):\n        run(interp, avm_class, code(\n            PUSHBYTE, 1,\n            CALLPROPVOID, u30(IDX_UNKNOWN), u30(0),\n            RETURNVALUE))\n```\n\nnewarray:\n\n```python\ndef test_opcode_newarray():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHBYTE, 1, PUSHBYTE, 2, NEWARRAY, u30(2), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == [1, 2]\n```\n\nfindpropstrict:\n\n```python\ndef test_findpropstrict_in_variables():\n    avm_class.variables['x'] = 5\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        FINDPROPSTRICT, u30(IDX_X), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 5\n\n\ndef test_findpropstrict_builtin_class():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        FINDPROPSTRICT, u30(IDX_STRING), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res is _builtin_classes['String']\n```\n\nfindproperty:\n\n```python\ndef test_findproperty_found_in_variables():\n    avm_class.variables['y'] = 1\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        FINDPROPERTY, u30(IDX_Y), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert isinstance(res, _ScopeDict)\n    assert res.avm_class is avm_class\n    assert res['y'] == 1\n\n\ndef test_findproperty_not_found_defaults_to_variables():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        FINDPROPERTY, u30(IDX_NOPE), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert isinstance(res, _ScopeDict)\n    assert res.avm_class is avm_class\n```\n\ngetlex:\n\n```python\ndef test_getlex_from_variables():\n    avm_class.variables['z'] = 7\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(GETLEX, u30(IDX_Z), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 7\n\n\ndef test_getlex_builtin_class():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(GETLEX, u30(IDX_STRING), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res is _builtin_classes['String']\n\n\ndef test_getlex_uninitialized():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(GETLEX, u30(IDX_NOPE), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res is undefined\n```\n\nsetproperty:\n\n```python\ndef test_setproperty_with_string_name():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        FINDPROPERTY, u30(IDX_NOPE),\n        PUSHBYTE, 5,\n        SETPROPERTY, u30(IDX_KEY2),\n        RETURNVOID))\n    assert res is undefined\n    assert avm_class.variables['key2'] == 5\n\n\ndef test_setproperty_with_multiname():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        FINDPROPERTY, u30(IDX_NOPE),\n        PUSHSTRING, u30(S_KEY),\n        PUSHBYTE, 5,\n        SETPROPERTY, u30(IDX_DYNAMIC),\n        RETURNVOID))\n    assert avm_class.variables['key'] == 5\n```\n\ngetlocal/setlocal:\n\n```python\ndef test_getlocal_setlocal():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHBYTE, 1, SETLOCAL, u30(1), GETLOCAL, u30(1), RETURNVALUE),\n        local_count=1)\n    assert res == 1\n```\n\ngetproperty:\n\n```python\ndef test_getproperty_length_string():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHSTRING, u30(S_ABC), GETPROPERTY, u30(IDX_LENGTH), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 3\n\n\ndef test_getproperty_length_list():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHBYTE, 1, PUSHBYTE, 2, NEWARRAY, u30(2),\n        GETPROPERTY, u30(IDX_LENGTH), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 2\n\n\ndef test_getproperty_static_property_on_class():\n    other = make_avm_class()\n    other.static_properties['sp'] = 42\n    interp._classes_by_name['MyClass'] = other\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        GETLEX, u30(IDX_MYCLASS), GETPROPERTY, u30(IDX_SP), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 42\n\n\ndef test_getproperty_member_on_scope_dict():\n    avm_class.variables['zz'] = 33\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        FINDPROPERTY, u30(IDX_NOPE), GETPROPERTY, u30(IDX_ZZ), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 33\n\n\ndef test_getproperty_member_default_undefined():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        FINDPROPERTY, u30(IDX_NOPE), GETPROPERTY, u30(IDX_ZZ), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res is undefined\n\n\ndef test_getproperty_index_access_on_list():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHBYTE, 1, PUSHBYTE, 2, NEWARRAY, u30(2),\n        PUSHBYTE, 1,\n        GETPROPERTY, u30(IDX_DYNAMIC),\n        RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 2\n```\n\ninitproperty:\n\n```python\ndef test_initproperty_with_string_name():\n    run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        FINDPROPERTY, u30(IDX_NOPE),\n        PUSHBYTE, 9,\n        INITPROPERTY, u30(IDX_IP),\n        RETURNVOID))\n    assert avm_class.variables['ip'] == 9\n\n\ndef test_initproperty_with_multiname():\n    run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        FINDPROPERTY, u30(IDX_NOPE),\n        PUSHSTRING, u30(S_KEY2),\n        PUSHBYTE, 9,\n        INITPROPERTY, u30(IDX_DYNAMIC),\n        RETURNVOID))\n    assert avm_class.variables['key2'] == 9\n```\n\nconvert_i:\n\n```python\ndef test_opcode_convert_i():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHSTRING, u30(S_42), CONVERT_I, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 42\n    assert isinstance(res, int)\n```\n\ncoerce:\n\n```python\ndef test_opcode_coerce():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHBYTE, 1, COERCE, u30(0), RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 1\n\n\ndef test_opcode_coerce_a():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHBYTE, 1, COERCE_A, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 1\n\n\ndef test_opcode_coerce_s():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHSTRING, u30(S_X), COERCE_S, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 'x'\n\n\ndef test_opcode_coerce_s_null():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHNULL, COERCE_S, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res is None\n```\n\ndecrement:\n\n```python\ndef test_opcode_decrement():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(PUSHBYTE, 5, DECREMENT, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 4\n```\n\ntypeof (parametrized):\n\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    'code_seq,expected',\n    [\n        (code(PUSHUNDEFINED, TYPEOF), 'undefined'),\n        (code(PUSHSTRING, u30(S_X), TYPEOF), 'String'),\n        (code(PUSHBYTE, 1, TYPEOF), 'Number'),\n        (code(PUSHNAN, TYPEOF), 'Number'),\n    ])\ndef test_opcode_typeof(code_seq, expected):\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    assert run(interp, avm_class, code_seq) == expected\n```\n\nArithmetic (parametrized):\n\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    'opcode,lhs,rhs,expected',\n    [\n        (ADD, 2, 3, 5),\n        (SUBTRACT, 5, 2, 3),\n        (MULTIPLY, 3, 4, 12),\n        (MODULO, 7, 3, 1),\n        (BITAND, 6, 3, 2),\n        (EQUALS, 1, 1, True),\n        (EQUALS, 1, 2, False),\n        (GREATEREQUALS, 5, 3, True),\n        (GREATEREQUALS, 3, 5, False),\n    ])\ndef test_binary_opcodes(opcode, lhs, rhs, expected):\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHBYTE, lhs, PUSHBYTE, rhs, opcode, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == expected\n```\n\nWait \u2014 BITAND asserts isinstance int \u2014 pushbyte gives int. Good. EQUALS with ints fine.\n\nString add:\n\n```python\ndef test_opcode_add_strings():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n        PUSHSTRING, u30(S_ABC), PUSHSTRING, u30(S_X), ADD, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 'abcx'\n```\n\nincrement_i:\n\n```python\ndef test_opcode_increment_i():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(PUSHBYTE, 4, INCREMENT_I, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert res == 5\n```\n\ngetlocal_n / setlocal_n:\n\n```python\ndef test_getlocal0_returns_variables():\n    res = run(interp, avm_class, code(GETLOCAL0, RETURNVALUE))\n    assert isinstance(res, _ScopeDict)\n    assert res.avm_class is avm_class\n\n\ndef test_setlocal_getlocal_short_forms():\n    for set_op, get_op, value, extra_locals in (\n            (SETLOCAL1, GETLOCAL1, 1, 1),\n            (SETLOCAL2, GETLOCAL2, 2, 2),\n            (SETLOCAL3, GETLOCAL3, 3, 3)):\n        interp = make_interp()\n        avm_class = make_avm_class()\n        res = run(interp, avm_class, code(\n            PUSHBYTE, value, set_op, get_op, RETURNVALUE),\n            local_count=extra_locals)\n        assert res == value\n```\n\nHmm, loop inside test \u2014 fine.\n\nUnsupported opcode:\n\n```python\ndef test_unsupported_opcode_raises():\n    interp = make_interp()\n    avm_class = make_avm_class()\n    with pytest.raises(NotImplementedError) as exc_info:\n        run(interp, avm_class, code(0xFF))\n    assert 'Unsupported opcode 255' in str(exc_info.value)\n```\n\nNow \u2014 wait, there's an issue with `run` when the code raises: `func(list(args))` raises, fine.\n\nAlso, one subtlety: in `test_callproperty_string_class_from_undefined`, findpropstrict 'String' \u2014 but wait, is 'String' in avm_class.variables? No. In constants? No. In _classes_by_name? We didn't add it. Good.\n\nBut hold on \u2014 in `test_findpropstrict_in_variables`, I set variables['x'] = 5 and findpropstrict IDX_X ('x'). reversed(scopes): variables first -> 'x' in variables -> res = variables. Then `if mname not in res and mname in _builtin_classes:` \u2014 'x' in res -> False -> else: stack.append(res['x']) = 5. Good, covers line 671 via else.\n\nAnd `test_findpropstrict_builtin_class` covers line 669.\n\nNow \u2014 potential problem: `_ScopeDict.__getitem__` fallback to constants. In `test_callproperty_on_scope_dict_constant`, obj['k'] -> not in dict -> constants['k'] = 42. Good.\n\nAnother subtlety: `findproperty` line 675-680: `for s in reversed(scopes): if mname in s: res = s; break; else: res = avm_class.variables`. For IDX_NOPE ('nope') \u2014 not in any scope -> res = avm_class.variables. Good.\n\nNow, `GETLEX` for 'MyClass': covered.\n\nNow, about `pushscope` \u2014 after pushscope, scopes has an extra element (the int 1). That doesn't affect subsequent ops in that test since we return right after.\n\nNow, `construct` \u2014 wait, I need to double-check `obj.avm_class.make_object()`. obj is _AVMClass_Object from constructproperty. Good.\n\nNow \u2014 one thing I should double check: `_AVMClass_Object` \u2014 does it have `avm_class` attribute? Yes per the snippet usage.\n\nNow, `StringClass` \u2014 need to confirm it exists at module level and `_builtin_classes` maps 'String' to it. get_info.\n\nAlso \u2014 `compat_str` is `str` (or unicode on Py2). Tests presumably run on Py3. Fine.\n\nNow, about `SWFInterpreter.__new__(SWFInterpreter)` \u2014 if `SWFInterpreter.__init__` is heavy, bypassing is good. But does `SWFInterpreter` define `__slots__`? Unlikely. Fine.\n\nNow, let me also think about whether `extract_function` uses `self._patched_functions.get((avm_class, func_name))` \u2014 requires `_AVMClass.__hash__`. _AVMClass defines __hash__ = hash(self.name) (probably) and __eq__. Two distinct classes with same name would be equal \u2014 my make_avm_class uses the same name '(test)' for multiple instances! If a test uses two classes both named '(test)'... In test_callproperty_on_avm_class_object, avm_class is '(test)' and other is '(test)' \u2014 the patched_functions dict key uses (avm_class, func_name) \u2014 but we don't use patched functions there. However, `_AVMClass.__eq__` comparing names could matter elsewhere? `if obj == StringClass` \u2014 StringClass name is something like '(String, True)'? If other class had same name as StringClass... not the case.\n\nBut to be safe, give distinct names: make_avm_class(name='(test)') and use make_avm_class('(other)') for the second class. Let me parameterize:\n\n```python\ndef make_avm_class(name='(test)'):\n    avm_class = _AVMClass(name, name)\n    ...\n```\n\nHmm, resolved_name = name? _AVMClass(name, resolved_name). resolved_name used for... repr maybe. Fine.\n\nWait, actually \u2014 does `_AVMClass.__eq__` get used in `if obj == StringClass`? obj is StringClass itself in our tests, so identity. Fine.\n\nBut also `interp._patched_functions.get((avm_class, func_name))` \u2014 tuple hashing requires avm_class hashable \u2014 _AVMClass defines __hash__ (since it defines __eq__, it must define __hash__ to be hashable; the real code does define __hash__). OK.\n\nNow, let me reconsider `test_extract_function_patched_function`: `interp._patched_functions[(avm_class, 'f')] = sentinel`. extract_function returns p. Good.\n\nNow \u2014 one more check on `run()`: `avm_class.methods[name] = _FakeMethod(...)`. If _AVMClass has no `methods` attribute, my make_avm_class adds it. But wait \u2014 maybe methods are stored differently, e.g., `avm_class.methods` is a dict created in __init__. get_info will confirm.\n\nAlso `_FakeMethod` needs `.code` and `.local_count` only. Good.\n\nNow, about `u30` encoding for values like 0: u30(0) -> bytes([0]). Decoder: reads byte 0, no continuation -> 0. Good.\n\nNow, `s24(2)` -> bytes [2,0,0]. Decoder reads 3 bytes -> 2. Good.\n\nNow \u2014 the `code()` helper: parts can be ints (single bytes) or bytes. Good.\n\nNow, let me also double check the `iftrue` offset math: code = [38, 17, 2,0,0, 36, 9, 72]. Positions: 0: PUSHTRUE; 1: IFTRUE; 2-4: s24; after reading, tell()=5; offset 2 -> 7 -> RETURNVALUE. Stack: [True]. Returns True. Good.\n\nFor not-taken: after iftrue, position 5: PUSHBYTE 9 (5,6), then 7: RETURNVALUE. Returns 9. Good.\n\nifeq: [36,1, 36,1, 19, 2,0,0, 36,9, 72]: positions: 0-1 pushbyte 1; 2-3 pushbyte 1; 4: IFEQ; 5-7: s24; tell=8; offset 2 -> 10 -> RETURNVALUE. Stack: [1,1] -> pop 1, pop 1 -> equal -> seek 10. Returns 1. Good.\n\nNot taken: values 1,2 -> not equal -> continue at 8: pushbyte 9 (8,9), returnvalue at 10. Returns 9. Good.\n\nNow `constructsuper`: [36,7, 36,1, 36,2, 73, u30(2), 36,3, 72]. constructsuper: arg_count=2; args = reversed([pop 2, pop 1]) = [1,2]; obj = pop 7. Then pushbyte 3, returnvalue -> 3. Good.\n\nNow `newarray` order: pushbyte 1, pushbyte 2 -> stack [1,2]. newarray 2: arr = [pop 2, pop 1] = [2,1]; arr = arr[::-1] = [1,2]. Good.\n\n`dup` then `callpropvoid reverse`: stack [1,2] -> newarray -> [1,2] on stack; dup -> [ [1,2], [1,2] ]; callpropvoid reverse 0: index u30, mname 'reverse', arg_count 0, args [], obj = pop -> the second copy; obj.reverse() -> that list becomes [2,1]. But the dup'd copy is the SAME list object (dup pushes same reference). So the remaining stack top is the same list, now [2,1]. returnvalue -> [2,1]. \n\nNow `getproperty` dynamic (_Multiname): pname = multinames[IDX_DYNAMIC] which is a _Multiname instance -> else branch: idx = stack.pop() (1); obj = stack.pop() ([1,2]); stack.append(obj[1]) = 2. Good.\n\nWait \u2014 careful: `elif isinstance(pname, compat_str):` \u2014 _Multiname is not str -> else branch. Good.\n\nBut hold on \u2014 for `setproperty`/`initproperty` with _Multiname: `if isinstance(idx, _Multiname): idx = stack.pop()`. Good.\n\nNow \u2014 is `_Multiname(0)` a valid constructor call? Need to check _Multiname.__init__ signature. get_info.\n\nNow, the `MULTINAMES` list contains a _Multiname instance at index 25. But `make_interp` copies the list \u2014 the same _Multiname instance shared across tests. That's fine (read-only usage... well, `idx = stack.pop()` replaces the local var, doesn't mutate the _Multiname). OK.\n\nHmm \u2014 wait, actually there might be an issue: in real parsing, multinames entries that are _Multiname have `.name` set etc. But the interpreter only checks `isinstance(pname, _Multiname)` / `isinstance(pname, compat_str)`. Fine.\n\nNow, `test_getlex_uninitialized`: getlex 'nope' -> scope = avm_class.variables (line 690); 'nope' in scope? No; in _builtin_classes? No -> res = undefined (line 699). Good.\n\nNow \u2014 `test_getlex_builtin_class`: getlex 'String' -> scope search: variables? no. constants? no. _classes_by_name? no -> scope = variables. 'String' in scope? no. 'String' in _builtin_classes? yes -> res = _builtin_classes['String']. Good.\n\nNow \u2014 `pushshort` u30(300): decoder must handle multi-byte. Good.\n\nNow, let me reconsider: are there any lines in 439-834 I haven't covered?\n\n- 439-441: patched. \u2713\n- 442-443: pyfunctions. \u2713\n- 444-445: classes_by_name. \u2713\n- 44