[1]) << 8) | (int(bs[2]) << 16)\n    if v & 0x800000:\n        v -= 0x1000000\n    return v\n```\n\nHmm, I need to check. Let me use get_info for `_u30`, `_s24`, `_read_byte`.\n\nActually, in youtube_dl/swfinterp.py:\n\n```python\ndef _read_byte(coder):\n    return coder.read(1)[0]\n\n\ndef _read_uint(coder):\n    n = 0\n    for i in range(5):\n        b = coder.read(1)[0]\n        n = (n << 7) | (b & 0x7f)\n        if not b & 0x80:\n            break\n    return n\n\n\ndef _s24(coder):\n    b3 = coder.read(3)\n    v = b3[0] | (b3[1] << 8) | (b3[2] << 16)\n    if v & 0x800000:\n        v = v - 0x1000000\n    return v\n```\n\nI'm not 100% sure. Let me query get_info.\n\nAlso `_u30`:\n\n```python\ndef _u30(coder):\n    v = _read_uint(coder)\n    assert v & 0xf0000000 == 0\n    return v\n```\n\nHmm. Let me just query.\n\nNow, the plan for building test bytecode. I'll write helper functions in the test module:\n\n```python\ndef u30_bytes(v):\n    # encode v as u30\n    out = bytearray()\n    while True:\n        b = v & 0x7f\n        v >>= 7\n        if v:\n            out.append(b | 0x80)\n        else:\n            out.append(b)\n            break\n    return bytes(out)\n\ndef s24_bytes(v):\n    if v < 0:\n        v += 0x1000000\n    return bytes([v & 0xff, (v >> 8) & 0xff, (v >> 16) & 0xff])\n```\n\nBut I must make sure these match the actual decoding functions. Let me check with get_info first.\n\nNow, creating the interpreter instance without running `__init__`:\n\n```python\ninterp = SWFInterpreter.__new__(SWFInterpreter)\ninterp._classes_by_name = {}\ninterp.constant_strings = ['hello', 'world', ...]\ninterp.multinames = ['length', 'split', ...]\ninterp._patched_functions = {}\n```\n\nWait \u2014 but `extract_function` references `self._patched_functions`, `self._classes_by_name`, `self.constant_strings`, `self.multinames`. That's all. So bypassing `__init__` is fine.\n\nBut hold on \u2014 maybe it's better to actually construct via `__init__` with a minimal ABC file? That's complex. Bypassing `__init__` is simpler and acceptable for coverage of lines 439-834.\n\nHmm, but the instructions say \"Create new pytest test functions that execute all missing lines and branches\". Using `__new__` is fine.\n\nNow, the fake method:\n\n```python\nclass FakeMethod(object):\n    def __init__(self, code, local_count=0):\n        self.code = code\n        self.local_count = local_count\n```\n\nAnd avm_class:\n\n```python\navm_class = _AVMClass('(no name)', 'SomeClass')\navm_class.methods['main'] = FakeMethod(code, local_count)\n```\n\nWait, does `_AVMClass` have a `methods` attribute? Let me check. In swfinterp.py:\n\n```python\nclass _AVMClass(object):\n    def __init__(self, name, resolved_name, class_body=None):\n        self.name = name\n        self.resolved_name = resolved_name\n        self.class_body = class_body\n        self.method_names = {}\n        self.method_pyfunctions = {}\n        self.static_properties = {}\n\n        self.variables = _ScopeDict(self)\n        self.constants = {}\n```\n\nHmm, I don't remember `methods` being in `__init__`. Let me check with get_info. Actually in the parsing code, methods are added: `avm_class.methods[method_name] = method` maybe. Let me check `_AVMClass` definition via get_info.\n\nLet me also check `_Multiname`:\n\n```python\nclass _Multiname(object):\n    def __init__(self, kind_name):\n        self.kind = kind_name\n        self.name = None\n        ...\n```\n\nOK, let me start by calling get_info on the relevant symbols. I'll batch the calls:\n\n- SWFInterpreter\n- _AVMClass\n- _AVMClass_Object\n- _ScopeDict\n- _Multiname\n- _Undefined\n- undefined\n- _builtin_classes\n- StringClass\n- _read_byte\n- _u30\n- _s24\n- extract_function\n\nLet me do that now.\n\nAfter getting info, I'll write the tests.\n\nTest plan (each test builds bytecode and runs `interp.extract_function(avm_class, 'main')` and asserts the result):\n\n1. `test_extract_function_patched`: set `interp._patched_function