o stack has 1, returns 1. \n\n- **17 iftrue**: pushtrue (38), iftrue +2 (17 s24(2)), pushbyte 9 (36 09), returnvalue (72). Returns True. Also test iftrue with false value: pushfalse, iftrue +2, pushbyte 9, returnvalue -> returns 9 (no jump). Both branches.\n\n- **18 iffalse**: pushfalse (39), iffalse +2, pushbyte 9, returnvalue -> returns False. And pushtrue, iffalse +2, pushbyte 9, returnvalue -> 9.\n\n- **19 ifeq**: pushbyte 1, pushbyte 1, ifeq +2, pushbyte 9, returnvalue -> 1. And non-equal: pushbyte 1, pushbyte 2, ifeq +2, pushbyte 9, returnvalue -> 9.\n\n- **20 ifne**: pushbyte 1, pushbyte 2, ifne +2, pushbyte 9, returnvalue -> 1. Equal case -> 9.\n\n- **21 iflt**: pushbyte 1 (value1), pushbyte 2 (value2), iflt +2, pushbyte 9, returnvalue -> 1 (since 1<2). Non-lt: pushbyte 2, pushbyte 1, iflt +2, pushbyte 9, returnvalue -> 9.\n\n- **32 pushnull**: pushnull (32), returnvalue (72) -> None.\n\n- **33 pushundefined**: pushundefined (33), returnvalue -> undefined. Assert `res is undefined`.\n\n- **36 pushbyte**: pushbyte 42, returnvalue -> 42.\n\n- **37 pushshort**: pushshort u30(300), returnvalue -> 300.\n\n- **38 pushtrue** -> True. **39 pushfalse** -> False. **40 pushnan** -> NaN (math.isnan).\n\n- **42 dup**: pushbyte 7, dup, returnvalue -> 7 (pops the dup). Fine.\n\n- **44 pushstring**: pushstring u30(idx), returnvalue -> interp.constant_strings[idx]. Set constant_strings = ['abc'].\n\n- **48 pushscope**: pushbyte 1, pushscope, returnvoid? returnvoid returns undefined. Actually to verify pushscope executed, we can then use findproperty/getlex... Simpler: pushbyte 1, pushscope (48), returnvalue (72) -> pops... wait pushscope pops the value. Then returnvalue pops from empty stack -> IndexError. So: pushbyte 1, dup, pushscope, returnvalue -> returns 1. Hmm, that covers pushscope line 519-520 (new_scope = stack.pop(); scopes.append(new_scope)). Good enough for line coverage.\n\n- **66 construct**: Need obj on stack with avm_class attribute. `obj.avm_class.make_obje